# e03_colour.gbnf: the colour the rule lit, as the three literals of rules_e03.c letter
# for letter, and one bounded reason. The reason is 10 to 120 characters from letters,
# digits, space, comma and full stop, so it cannot carry a quote, a brace or a newline;
# the object closes only after it. The stub expands the first alternative on every
# path and a character class to nothing, so in CI the answer is
# {"colour":"GREEN","reason":""}, which the oracle file expects on every row. The reason
# is scored by projects/e03-led-explainer/tools/reason_check.py: it must name the field
# the rule triggered on, level or slope. ws admits spaces and tabs, never a newline.
root   ::= "{" ws "\"colour\"" ws ":" ws colour ws "," ws "\"reason\"" ws ":" ws reason ws "}"
colour ::= "\"GREEN\"" | "\"YELLOW\"" | "\"RED\""
reason ::= "\"" [a-zA-Z0-9 ,.]{10,120} "\""
ws     ::= [ \t]*
